Despite the significant advantages of waste bioconversion technologies using insects—particularly H. illucens larvae—the practical implementation of this innovation faces several serious challenges and limitations. These concerns technical, economic, regulatory, and environmental aspects. Bioconversion processes encounter several technical obstacles. The variability in the composition of organic waste complicates the standardization of processing parameters, as different types of waste require individualized treatment conditions (Table 14).
